        "content": "# Expert K-12 math tutor\n\nYou are an expert K-12 math tutor.\n\nYour goal is **not** to get the student to a correct answer — it is to build\ndeeper understanding the student can apply on their own.\n\n### The core dial: scaffold ↔ rigor\n\nEvery moment is a choice between adding **support** (a scaffold, to make the task\napproachable) and pushing for **rigor** (a harder task, a justification, a\ntransfer to a new problem).\n\nTwo failure modes bracket the right move:\n\n- **Over-scaffolding** — you do the thinking, give away the answer or the\n  operation, or help before the student has shown a need. This is the single\n  most common tutoring failure. Avoid it.\n- **Missed chances to push for rigor** — you miss chances to turn the dial\n  toward a more rigorous form of questioning by accepting an immediate correct\n  answer or re-teaching a skill the student has already mastered.\n\nThe goal is to stay in the student's zone of proximal development by:\n- Scaffolding for access when the content is challenging for the student.\n- Pushing for rigor when the student masters more basic expressions of a concept.\n\n### Context\n\nYou have the following metadata about the student: Platform: tutoring_provider_a\n\n### Sending multiple messages\n\nTo break up your response over multiple messages, use [NEW_MESSAGE]. The system will separate your response into multiple messages to the student.\n\nHere is the conversation so far:\n\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 25 seconds]\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE] The student's video feed disappears, and a message \"Jayden has left\" appears. The tutor's video feed disappears, and a message \"Ms. Rivera has left\" appears.\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 72 seconds] The screen shows a whiteboard with a drawing of a cat-like figure made of circles, ovals, and triangles.\nTurn 1. TUTOR: Hey Jayden.\nTurn 2. STUDENT: Not yet. You have to test.\nTurn 3. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 17 seconds]\nTurn 3. STUDENT: Hi.\nTurn 4. TUTOR: Hey Jayden. How's it going?\nTurn 5. STUDENT: Good.\nTurn 6. TUTOR: Good?\nTurn 7. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 4 seconds]\nTurn 7. TUTOR: How was your weekend?\nTurn 8. STUDENT: Good.\nTurn 9. TUTOR: Yeah?\nTurn 10. TUTOR: What are you up to now that summer school's over?\nTurn 11. STUDENT: I I go to summer camp now.\nTurn 12. TUTOR: Oh, summer camp? Nice.\nTurn 13. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 2 seconds]\nTurn 13. TUTOR: What do you guys do in summer camp?\nTurn 14. STUDENT: Play board games most of the time.\nTurn 15. TUTOR: Yeah?\nTurn 16. TUTOR: Do you like it?\nTurn 17. STUDENT: Yeah.\nTurn 18. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 3 seconds]\nTurn 18. TUTOR: Um, what board games do you play?\nTurn 19. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 5 seconds]\nTurn 19. STUDENT: I usually play like card games like Uno.\nTurn 20. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 6 seconds]\nTurn 20. TUTOR: Nice.\nTurn 21. TUTOR: What kind of card games?\nTurn 22. STUDENT: Uno.\nTurn 23. TUTOR: Uno? I love Uno.\nTurn 24. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 5 seconds]\nTurn 24. TUTOR: Okay, cool. Do you want to get started?\nTurn 25. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 3 seconds]\nTurn 25. TUTOR: Do you want me to share or do you want to share?\nTurn 26. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 8 seconds]\nTurn 26. TUTOR: Do you want me to share?\nTurn 27. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 2 seconds]\nTurn 27. STUDENT: Yeah.\nTurn 28. TUTOR: Okay, give me one sec. I'll sign in and get it up.\nTurn 29. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 27 seconds]\nTurn 29. TUTOR: Okay, can you see the screen?\nTurn 30. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 8 seconds] [SCREEN UPDATE] Tutor shares their screen, showing the a learning platform dashboard. A banner at the top reads \"Summer Club is LIVE! Answer the QOTD for your chance to win a prize in the weekly raffle! See results\".\nTurn 30. STUDENT: Yeah.\nTurn 31. TUTOR: Yeah? Okay, cool.\nTurn 32. TUTOR: Um, what do you want to do? Do you want to look at your avatar or the prizes?\nTurn 33. STUDENT: Um, the the the weekly raffle. That's what it says.\nTurn 34. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 3 seconds]\nTurn 34. TUTOR: Oh, this one?\nTurn 35. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 6 seconds]\nTurn 35. STUDENT: There's a chance to win a prize.\nTurn 36. TUTOR: Mmm.\nTurn 37. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 3 seconds]\nTurn 37. TUTOR: Let's see. Let me share this other tab with you. Okay, give me one sec. I'll share my whole screen.\nTurn 38. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 4 seconds] [SCREEN INTERACTION: tutor - clicking] Clicks the \"See results\" button on the banner.\nTurn 38. TUTOR: See results.\nTurn 39. TUTOR: You're talking...\nTurn 40. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 4 seconds]\nTurn 40. STUDENT: Yeah. Yeah.\nTurn 41. TUTOR: You're talking about this?\nTurn 42. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE: Opens new tab] A new browser tab opens with the title \"Summer Club Results\". The tutor then re-shares their entire screen, which shows a \"hall-of-mirrors\" effect before settling on the a learning platform dashboard.\n[SCREEN INTERACTION: tutor - clicking] Clicks the \"See results\" button again.\nTurn 42. STUDENT: What is Summer Club?\nTurn 43. TUTOR: See results.\nTurn 44. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE: Opens new tab] The \"Summer Club Results\" tab is shown. The student is reading the page.\n[SCREEN INTERACTION: tutor - highlighting text] Highlights the paragraph under \"What are the prizes?\".\nTurn 44. STUDENT: What's a voucher?\nTurn 45. TUTOR: Every time you complete a question of the day, you'll earn one entry into our weekly prize draw. Each week we'll randomly pick three lucky students to each win a twenty pound voucher.\nTurn 46. STUDENT: What's a voucher?\nTurn 47. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 35 seconds] [SCREEN INTERACTION: tutor - highlighting text] Highlights the paragraph under the \"Don't see your Question of the Day?\" heading.\nTurn 47. TUTOR: Don't see your question of the day? You need to complete at least one topic quiz on a learning platform before you're given a question of the day. Make sure you complete a topic quiz first.\nTurn 48. STUDENT: Wait. That's what it says?\nTurn 49. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 14 seconds]\nTurn 49. TUTOR: Okay, let me share just my tab again so that way it's not infinite.\nTurn 50. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE: Screen share changes 